WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.310
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:03.860
 We live in strange times.

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:08.596
The housing bubble
burst-- rise of China--

00:00:08.596 --> 00:00:09.720
and the rise of inequality.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:10.803
Health is a very big deal.

00:00:10.803 --> 00:00:12.070
Taxes are a front rank issue.

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.330
Blue-collar jobs were lost.

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:14.900
Two groups have
been left behind.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:18.380
But it's a complicated story.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.750
Instead of saying, ah,
it's a complicated world,

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:24.180
I don't get it, say, all right,
let me try to figure this out.

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:27.380
Let me make sense of this.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:29.510
Doing economics
requires stepping back

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:32.870
from all of the details to say,
what is the essential here?

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:34.200
What is the story?

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.010
It's about people.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:36.320
It's not about money.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:39.470
And it ends up being
about what people do.

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:43.400
Really good economics has
a kind of beauty to it.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.320
And it comes down to
just two principles.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:47.690
Hundred-dollar bills don't
lie on the street very long.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:50.080
The other is, every
sale is also a purchase.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:50.970
Things add up.

00:00:54.515 --> 00:00:56.390
What you're going to
learn here in this class

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:58.750
is how to think
like an economist.

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:01.160
Health care in America
is an economic issue.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:04.280
Left to its own devices, private
health insurance actually

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:06.380
just doesn't work.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:10.370
The crisis of 2008 wasn't as
bad as the Great Depression.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:13.690
And if you ask why, well,
because we learned something.

00:01:16.335 --> 00:01:18.460
It's never been more
important to educate yourself.

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:19.924
There isn't an
establishment that

00:01:19.924 --> 00:01:21.340
knows what it's
doing and is going

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:23.130
to get us through all of this.

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:26.430
It's going to have
to come from you.

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:28.770
There's no guarantee
that good ideas prevail.

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:31.230
But if you don't try to
have those good ideas

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:34.170
and get them out there, then,
of course, they won't prevail.

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:38.130
Keep on plugging, and don't
let the crazies grind you down.

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:42.110
I'm Paul Krugman, and
this is my MasterClass.

